Implement native iOS voice dictation for the existing ChatPop message composer.

IMPORTANT:
This is NOT Voice Chat.
This feature is speech-to-text dictation for the normal chat input.

Do not redesign unrelated parts of ChatPop.

==================================================
1. TRIGGER
==================================================

When the user taps the microphone icon inside the normal ChatPop message composer:

Open a native iOS-style voice dictation sheet/modal from the bottom.

Do NOT immediately send a message.

==================================================
2. DICTATION SHEET
==================================================

The sheet should look similar in interaction to the reference screenshot, but use ChatPop's own design.

Use:

- Dark / black background
- Rounded top corners
- Native iOS presentation
- Medium ChatPop blue accent
- White primary text
- Gray secondary elements

At the top-right:
- X button to cancel/close

The sheet should support swipe-down dismissal where appropriate.

==================================================
3. LIVE SPEECH-TO-TEXT
==================================================

As soon as the sheet opens and microphone permission is available:

Start listening to the user's microphone.

Use native iOS speech recognition.

Prefer Apple's native frameworks:

- AVAudioSession
- AVAudioEngine
- SFSpeechRecognizer
- SFSpeechAudioBufferRecognitionRequest

Request the required microphone and speech-recognition permissions properly.

Do NOT upload audio to our backend for this feature unless explicitly needed later.

==================================================
4. LIVE TRANSCRIPT
==================================================

Display the user's recognized speech LIVE inside the sheet.

Example:

User says:

"Can you help me plan a trip to Japan?"

While speaking, the text should progressively appear:

"Can..."
"Can you help..."
"Can you help me plan a trip..."
"Can you help me plan a trip to Japan?"

Use partial recognition results.

The displayed transcript should update continuously while the user speaks.

==================================================
5. AUDIO WAVEFORM
==================================================

Show a horizontal animated waveform/audio-level visualization similar to the reference.

It should:

- Move/react while the user is speaking
- Become larger when the voice is louder
- Become smaller when the voice is quieter
- Use ChatPop blue / blue-gray tones
- Stay subtle and premium

IMPORTANT:
Do NOT use a fake looping animation.

Drive the waveform using REAL microphone audio level / metering from AVAudioEngine.

The waveform does not need to represent exact audio samples visually, but its amplitude should react to actual microphone input.

==================================================
6. INSERT BUTTON
==================================================

At the bottom of the sheet add a large button:

Insert

Use ChatPop medium blue.

Behavior:

If there is recognized text:
- Insert button is enabled.

If transcript is empty:
- Insert button is disabled.

When the user taps Insert:

1. Stop speech recognition.
2. Stop microphone capture.
3. Close the dictation sheet.
4. Insert the recognized text into the existing ChatPop message input.
5. DO NOT automatically send the message.

The user should be able to edit the inserted text before sending.

Example:

Voice:
"Explain quantum physics simply"

After Insert:

Message ChatPop:
"Explain quantum physics simply"

Then the user can edit it or press Send.

==================================================
7. CANCEL / X
==================================================

When the user taps X:

- Stop recording
- Stop speech recognition
- Discard the current transcript
- Close the sheet
- Do not modify the chat input

==================================================
8. EXISTING TEXT
==================================================

If the message composer already contains text before opening dictation:

DO NOT delete it.

When Insert is tapped, append the dictated text intelligently.

Example:

Existing:
"Please explain"

Dictated:
"this image for me"

Result:
"Please explain this image for me"

Handle spacing correctly.

==================================================
9. PERMISSIONS
==================================================

Add/configure the required iOS permission descriptions:

- Microphone permission
- Speech Recognition permission

Use clear ChatPop-specific descriptions.

Do not crash if permission is denied.

If permission is denied:
show a clear message explaining that microphone/speech permission is required and allow the user to open iOS Settings if appropriate.

==================================================
10. STATES
==================================================

Support these UI states:

- Requesting permission
- Listening
- Recognizing
- Transcript available
- No speech detected
- Permission denied
- Recognition unavailable/error

Do not show raw Apple/native error codes to the user.

==================================================
11. LANGUAGE
==================================================

Use the user's current app/device language where practical for speech recognition.

Structure the implementation so later ChatPop can explicitly choose recognition languages such as:

- English
- Arabic
- Swedish

Do not hard-code English-only recognition.

==================================================
12. NATIVE IOS
==================================================

This feature should use REAL native iOS microphone and speech-recognition APIs.

Do not simulate speech recognition in JavaScript.

If the existing React + Capacitor composer needs a native bridge:

Create the minimum clean Capacitor native bridge required.

Keep the existing ChatPop iOS project.

Do NOT:

- recreate /ios
- run npx cap add ios
- change Bundle Identifier
- change Development Team
- change Signing

==================================================
13. PRIVACY / CLEANUP
==================================================

When recording stops:

- remove AVAudioEngine taps correctly
- stop the audio engine
- end the recognition request
- release recognition tasks
- restore the audio session appropriately

Opening and closing dictation repeatedly must not create duplicate audio sessions or crashes.

==================================================
14. REAL IPHONE TEST
==================================================

Test on the existing real iPhone:

1. Tap microphone
2. Sheet opens
3. Speak
4. Waveform reacts to actual voice
5. Transcript appears live
6. Tap Insert
7. Text appears in ChatPop composer
8. Text is NOT automatically sent
9. Reopen microphone and repeat
10. Tap X and confirm transcript is discarded
11. Deny permission and verify graceful handling

When finished, STOP and report:

- Native iOS APIs used
- Files changed
- Permission keys added
- How waveform levels are calculated
- How transcript is passed back to the existing composer
- Whether it was tested successfully on the real iPhone
